        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0992484c-d28b-5f78-9dd0-4da88a691900",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Frank Lloyd Wright, Theodore A. Pappas, Gerald B. Tonkens, Beverley Tonkens\n- Places: St. Louis, Missouri, Amberley Village, Hamilton County, Ohio\n- Projects: Theodore A. Pappas House, Gerald B. and Beverley Tonkens House\n- Concepts: Usonian houses, Usonian Automatics\n\nFacts:\n- In 1954, Frank Lloyd Wright designed the Gerald B. and Beverley Tonkens House as a single-story private residence.\n- The Gerald B. and Beverley Tonkens House is located in Amberley Village in Hamilton County, Ohio.\n- The Theodore A. Pappas House is a Frank Lloyd Wright-designed Usonian house in St. Louis, Missouri.\n- The Theodore A. Pappas House is a rambling four-bedroom house.\n- The Theodore A. Pappas House is the second-largest Usonian Automatic built, after the Gerald B. and Beverley Tonkens House.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "be8ad891-93c9-50bb-a3db-226541abe327",
